  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    [
      "He comes to us on another ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombre", "en": "man" },
      "'s back. That is the first thing. A ",
      { "id": "cacique", "es": "cacique", "en": "chief" },
      " does not walk to meet strangers. He is carried, and the ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombre", "en": "man" },
      " who carries him holds his head high. In front of them come ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombres", "en": "men" },
      " playing ",
      { "id": "flauta", "es": "flautas", "en": "flutes" },
      " made of reed, and behind them come many people. The ",
      { "id": "musica", "es": "música", "en": "music" },
      " reaches us before they do."
    ],
    [
      "The ",
      { "id": "cacique", "es": "cacique", "en": "chief" },
      " wears the ",
      { "id": "piel", "es": "piel", "en": "hide" },
      " of a ",
      { "id": "ciervo", "es": "ciervo", "en": "deer" },
      ", painted. The ",
      { "id": "color", "es": "colores", "en": "colors" },
      " are laid on in lines and marks, and I do not know what the ",
      { "id": "color", "es": "colores", "en": "colors" },
      " mean. His name is Dulchanchellin. The ",
      { "id": "gobernador", "es": "gobernador", "en": "governor" },
      " goes to him and they talk with their hands for a long time. I stand close and write down what I understand, which is little."
    ],
    [
      "This much is clear. The Apalachee are his ",
      { "id": "enemigo", "es": "enemigos", "en": "enemies" },
      ". He wants us to go to Apalachee, and he will come with us, and his people will come with us. An ",
      { "id": "enemigo", "es": "enemigo", "en": "enemy" },
      " of your ",
      { "id": "enemigo", "es": "enemigo", "en": "enemy" },
      " is a friend, in Florida as in Castile. The ",
      { "id": "gobernador", "es": "gobernador", "en": "governor" },
      " gives him beads and small bells. The ",
      { "id": "cacique", "es": "cacique", "en": "chief" },
      " takes off the ",
      { "id": "piel", "es": "piel", "en": "hide" },
      " of the ",
      { "id": "ciervo", "es": "ciervo", "en": "deer" },
      " and gives it to the ",
      { "id": "gobernador", "es": "gobernador", "en": "governor" },
      ". It is still warm."
    ],
    [
      "We walk with them the rest of the day, ",
      { "id": "norte", "es": "norte", "en": "north" },
      ", through the same ",
      { "id": "arena", "es": "arena", "en": "sand" },
      " and the same ",
      { "id": "pino", "es": "pinos", "en": "pines" },
      ", with the ",
      { "id": "sol", "es": "sol", "en": "sun" },
      " on our helmets. The ",
      { "id": "flauta", "es": "flautas", "en": "flutes" },
      " play the whole way. I have heard ",
      { "id": "musica", "es": "música", "en": "music" },
      " in the ",
      { "id": "tormenta", "es": "tormenta", "en": "storm" },
      " at Trinidad, played by nobody, and I hear it here, played by ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombres", "en": "men" },
      " who want us to fight their war. I do not know which frightens me more. I write it down anyway: ",
      { "id": "flauta", "es": "flautas", "en": "flutes" },
      " of reed, a painted ",
      { "id": "piel", "es": "piel", "en": "hide" },
      ", a ",
      { "id": "cacique", "es": "cacique", "en": "chief" },
      " on a ",
      { "id": "hombre", "es": "hombre", "en": "man" },
      "'s back, and three hundred Spaniards walking behind him toward the ",
      { "id": "oro", "es": "oro", "en": "gold" },
      "."
    ],
    [
      "Ahead of us, the ",
      { "id": "cacique", "es": "cacique", "en": "chief" },
      " says with his hands, there is a ",
      { "id": "rio", "es": "río", "en": "river" },
      ". A big one. Bigger than the last. He does not say how we will cross it, and we do not ask, because the ",
      { "id": "guia", "es": "guías", "en": "guides" },
      " we took at the last ",
      { "id": "rio", "es": "río", "en": "river" },
      " are walking beside him now, and they are not looking at us."
    ]
  ],
